usage: c500_paged_decode_harness.py [-h] [--library LIBRARY] [--cases CASES]
                                    [--seed SEED]
                                    [--lengths {boundary,random,full}]
                                    [--length-values LENGTH_VALUES]
                                    [--full-length] [--benchmark]
                                    [--warmup WARMUP]
                                    [--iterations ITERATIONS]
                                    [--samples SAMPLES]

Local GPU correctness harness for the XPUOJ paged-KV decode kernel. This loads
a MACA-built shared object with ctypes, invokes its ``run_kernel`` entry point
with the exact OJ ABI, and compares against the installed
``flash_attn_with_kvcache`` reference. Test shapes are obtained exclusively
from :mod:`c500_case_manifest`, which parses an accepted OJ SPJ response.
Examples: tools/build_local_maca.sh solutions/cuda_maca_optimized.cpp
build/cuda_maca_optimized.so python tests/c500_paged_decode_harness.py
--library build/cuda_maca_optimized.so python
tests/c500_paged_decode_harness.py --cases 7,9 --benchmark

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --library LIBRARY
  --cases CASES
  --seed SEED
  --lengths {boundary,random,full}
  --length-values LENGTH_VALUES
                        comma-separated exact cache lengths; each value is
                        broadcast to the selected case's whole batch and
                        tested in the same process
  --full-length         run every selected case at cache capacity (equivalent
                        to --lengths full)
  --benchmark
  --warmup WARMUP
  --iterations ITERATIONS
  --samples SAMPLES
